{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1390581-the-limitations-of-a-paradigm","id":1390581,"title":"The Limitations of a Paradigm","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-21T10:49:17-07:00","id":1390581,"title":"The Limitations of a Paradigm","content":"For the last little while I have had an idea for a Hollower Chaos Magician on the back-burner, as a potential PC in a game of M:tAs or maybe as a self-insert NPC if I'm running the game instead. I've had a lot of fun working on ideas for his Focus/Paradigm, but there's a particular question that I haven't been able to resolve, and I was hoping for some input from people with more experience. The basic premise of the Paradigm is pretty Purple; everything is some form of Energy (Prime), and everything is connected (Correspondence); Magic(k) is learning how to use the Energy of Belief/Will (Mind) to manipulate Prime, using Correspondence connections to 'direct' or 'focus' it.<br /> <br /> While that very rough outline provides a Paradigm that is capable of almost anything, the particular details of his specific arcane theories end up creating some constraints. In his conception, Physical and Mental/Spiritual qualities are distinct &quot;modes&quot; or &quot;states&quot; of Prime, with direction interaction between the two being complicated and typically mediated by acting upon the more foundational Prime. I imagine Mind being his &quot;dominant&quot; Sphere because Mind acting directly upon Mind makes sense to him, while a lot of his other Effects would involve Entropy (manipulating chance through subtle manipulation of the underlying Prime). But I imagine his Paradigm having a lot of trouble with Vulgar physical effects, especially related to Forces and Matter; I don't see this guy tossing lightning bolts at people or turning lead into gold. Similarly, while I imagine Correspondence playing a huge part in his Magical Theory, the more Vulgar aspects of the Sphere (teleportation, warping space) don't seem to mesh well with the concept.<br /> <br /> My question is, do you think that hard limits on the kinds of Effects a Mage can learn to cast within their Paradigm are a good thing?<br /> <br /> Should things like Teleportation or Fireballs be impossible for him unless he hypothetically manages to Ascend?<br /> <br /> Or is it more appropriate that his Paradigm should, eventually, be able to accommodate these Effects?<br /> <br /> The question is relevant mostly in the consideration of the relationship between his Instruments and Effects. I'm wondering if I need to consider which/how many Instruments he might need to perform such Effects, compared to other Spheres which come more naturally to him. My original plan was that these kinds of Effects would require multiple Instruments and considerably more prep time for him to achieve, and reaching the point where he can just &quot;will&quot; such Effects into being would take much longer. Obviously the Spheres he actually learns will place practical limitations on what he can achieve in-game, but this question is about what is theoretically possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-21T11:56:40-07:00","id":1390598,"title":"","content":"I would suggest going through each sphere and explain how the pc views it through the lens of their paradigm. Somethings might be beyond their understanding","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-21T12:40:56-07:00","id":1390603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1390581-the-limitations-of-a-paradigm#post1390581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My question is, do you think that hard limits on the kinds of Effects a Mage can learn to cast within their Paradigm are a good thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>By definition, Paradigm imposed limits are going to be <b>soft</b>. Very rarely they're hard (mystic vs. technomancers being an example of a hard limitation tied to the Focus)<br /> <br /> &quot;I don't see my mage doing X&quot; it's a perfectly reasonable tought (and does limit what you can do)...but afterwards you could always discover or imagine a way of doing X that makes perfect sense for your mage. So it's better not to see these Effects as being &quot;off bounds&quot;, you've just yet to imagine how to do them within your Paradigm<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Should things like Teleportation or Fireballs be impossible for him unless he hypothetically manages to Ascend? </div> </div> </div>If I had a character with such a Paradigm, I would say that my mage uses his application of Will to affect the Energy surrounding a target, transforming it into fire. Fire it's just an expression of Prime like everything else, hence there should be a way to &quot;get&quot; from Prime-energy to more mundane fire. If I can alter the first, I should be able to get the latter. Easy peasy<br /> <br /> Teleportation would be more esoteric on the worldview I'm thinking off. I could explain it as altering the way my Energy/Pattern relates to other stuff - if part of my Focus it's &quot;everything it's connected&quot;, I should be able to change the way these connections interact (as I'm doing magick here, not merely describing how things factually work). If I can do that, I can decide to interact with my room from anywhere. From that to teleportation it's semantics: I choose to interac &quot;totally&quot; with my room, with my whole body.<br /> <br /> In general I think you should try to be creative to explain all kinds of effects. Only don't do them if you really think it doesn't mesh with the style of your character.<br /> My experience in Mage it's that I can *explain* almost every effect within my paradigm, but I can't always *do* everything because the way my character would do that it's too complex/impractical/doesn't have the right tools (the bane of technomancers :P ) . The Instrument it's usually more limiting that the Paradigm<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or is it more appropriate that his Paradigm should, eventually, be able to accommodate these Effects?<br /> <br /> The question is relevant mostly in the consideration of the relationship between his Instruments and Effects. I'm wondering if I need to consider which/how many Instruments he might need to perform such Effects, compared to other Spheres which come more naturally to him. My original plan was that these kinds of Effects would require multiple Instruments and considerably more prep time for him to achieve, and reaching the point where he can just &quot;will&quot; such Effects into being would take much longer. Obviously the Spheres he actually learns will place practical limitations on what he can achieve in-game, but this question is about what is theoretically possible. </div> </div> </div>I'm a firm believer that *anything* should be at least theoretically possible for any Mage (well, almost anything). The particulars are up to you, but I think that approach it's perfectly sensible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 05-21-2020, 03:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-21T13:11:13-07:00","id":1390608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1390581-the-limitations-of-a-paradigm?p=1390598#post1390598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would suggest going through each sphere and explain how the pc views it through the lens of their paradigm. Somethings might be beyond their understanding</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Are you asking me to provide an overview here to help readers resolve the question, or to go through each Sphere and consider it personally?<br /> <br /> If you're simply asking me to consider things from that perspective to find my answer, I already have, and the resulting uncertainty is what I'm hoping to get help with :P<br /> <br /> I haven't figured everything out yet, but I can provide a rough outline of my ideas below, if it would help?<br /> <br /> The simpler answer is that his Paradigm can conceive of the theoretical way to make it happen, but contains other constraints that might make such things practically impossible for him.<br /> <br /> Roughly how I'm conceiving things is that all magick starts with Mind; either Mind energy acts on other Mind energies (producing Mind effects), or acts on Prime to make other things possible (all Prime is interconnected = Correspondence; subtle alterations to the underlying Prime manipulating chance = Entropy). But to make the kind of large-scale alterations to physical phenomena produced by higher-level Matter and Forces Effects, or the more Vulgar applications of Time and Correspondence, requires a lot more raw 'power' than the subtle 'pokes' that are employed to achieve Entropy Effects. Spirit is kind of a funny thing, in that I imagine him not having it a part of his Paradigm initially, but being very easy to 'fit in' once he is exposed to the concepts.<br /> <br /> I suppose my question breaks down to which of three options is the best fit for the setting, or the most interesting:<br /> <br /> a) Accepting the Limits of the Paradigm: certain kinds of Effects will remain impossible unless/until he Ascends, because his Paradigm simply cannot accept that he can generate/wield/whatever the power necessary for Vulgar Pattern Effects.<br /> <br /> b) Shedding (the limits of) The Paradigm: his Paradigm grows more Purple, freeing him from the constraints that make certain kinds of will-working more difficult; this essentially takes the form of realizing that his beliefs about how his Paradigm works are wrong in some way.<br /> <br /> c) Deepening the Paradigm: rather than becoming more Purple in the sense of &quot;growing out&quot; of the weaknesses; he never stops believing that certain types of Effects are more difficult, but instead comes to believe that his own growing power/knowledge makes things possible that previously weren't.<br /> <br /> In a way, I'm wondering which of these answers is the most likely to be true within the &quot;canon&quot; of the setting? Using the Traditions as an example, some seem really well-equipped to include almost any kind of Sphere or Effect (e.g. the Hermetics), while others seem like they might have some serious limitations built in (e.g. Akashic alchemist?). Every option seems feasible, but I'm wondering what people feel about the flavour of each option? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-21T14:08:02-07:00","id":1390620,"title":"","content":"In my opinion, how hard the paradigm limit is should be more dependent on the mage's personality and how rigid or creative the person's thinking than anything else. Sure there are tons of ways to explain something, but would the person focus on what he or she understands, or add to their understanding and continually modify their mental model of magick and reality, or are they the type that can change their mind or believe in multiple conflicting models of understanding?<br /> <br /> As something of a mental exercise, I once tried to figure out how a specific akashic character I made with the idea of &quot;harmony of mind body and spirit to access the macrocosm through mastery of the macrocosm&quot; as a source of magick would work. <br /> <br /> Naturally, the mage had mind, spirit, and life. <br /> <br /> The mage would be inclined to develop mind up to 4 for astral travel, life 3 for enhanced physical capabilities, and spirit 3 to gain mastery of the spiritual self before even considering branching out to other spheres. <br /> <br /> At that point an understanding of the astral and the akashic records as something connected to one's self and to all other things could lead to an understanding of correspondence, entropy, and time, whilst a more comprehensive look at what binds the mind, body, and spirit together would lead to a greater understanding of prime. Matter and forces would probably remain elusive unless some experience highlighted their link to the microcosm of one's own mind body and spirit, perhaps by repeated interaction with the body's use of force on matter.<br /> <br /> Most likely, the character with mind 4, life 3, and spirit 3 would then either branch to correspondence 3 and entropy 3, or prime 5, or matter 2 and forces 3, or else simply bring life mind and spirit to 5 each. Then the character would probably alternate between Arete increase and branching out to increase mastery of spheres. <br /> <br /> This would be different for other characters but I'm guessing will follow a similar idea of development based on how the character thinks.<br /> <br /> Edit: I meant access of the macrocosm through the mastery of microcosm up there. Lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12480,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","user":"Spacecat","date":". 05-21-2020, 06:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-21T14:35:38-07:00","id":1390627,"title":"","content":"Thank you for your response, Aleph! I thought about editing in a response to your points, but I feel like I covered most of it responding to Dwight anyways <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Your response is also really helpful Spacecat. I very much imagine this character as a syncretist who eagerly tries to accommodate other perspectives into his own Paradigm, to the point where he might get in trouble with some of them for &quot;stealing&quot; their ideas ^_^; Using your example of acquiring knowledge of other Spheres after developing their talents in more familiar fields, an understanding of Spirit might be what expands his perspective to the point of influencing physical phenomena. I just need to decide where Spirit fits into his metaphysics; will he view Spirit as a subset of Mind/psychic phenomena, or more see it as a third &quot;mode/state&quot; of Prime that fits somewhere between his Physical/Mental dichotomy?<br /> <br /> P.S. That last question is just me thinking 'out loud'; I'm happy to hear any thoughts people have, but I don't need help figuring it out ^_^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","user":"Kharnov","date":". 05-21-2020, 05:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-21T15:37:49-07:00","id":1390636,"title":"","content":"Maybe spirit could be thought of as something like thought-forms given energy (Prime) but lacking the solidity of matter (possibly opening up the exploration of matter, life, and forces once spirit and prime are more known since these can be thought of as different variations of prime energy configuration) maybe?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-21T15:56:25-07:00","id":1390641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacecat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1390581-the-limitations-of-a-paradigm?p=1390636#post1390636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe spirit could be thought of as something like thought-forms given energy (Prime) but lacking the solidity of matter (possibly opening up the exploration of matter, life, and forces once spirit and prime are more known since these can be thought of as different variations of prime energy configuration) maybe?</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> The analogy that current represents my best theory is that Prime = atoms, while Forces/Matter/Life are comparable to solids, Spirit to fluids, and Mind to gases; different states of the same fundamental substance. I was also thinking that Life might be a bit easier for him to work with, so it could also serve as a good 'bridge Sphere' to Forces and Matter, like Spirit <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As demonstrated above, there's a lot of crossover between metaphysical/philosophical concepts and more scientific ones within his framework; E = MC-squared is as much an influence on his 'Prime is everything' theory as New-Agey &quot;energy&quot; concepts. He'd probably make a good NWO/Syndicate member if he wasn't extremely anti-authoritarian.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-22T08:54:18-07:00","id":1390789,"title":"","content":"I want to play a character who picks up magic from movies, TV, video games, and tabletop RPGs.<br /> <br /> Edit: and novels and comic books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-22T09:01:43-07:00","id":1390791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1390581-the-limitations-of-a-paradigm#post1390581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> (...)<br /> <br /> The question is relevant mostly in the consideration of the relationship between his Instruments and Effects. I'm wondering if I need to consider which/how many Instruments he might need to perform such Effects, compared to other Spheres which come more naturally to him. My original plan was that these kinds of Effects would require multiple Instruments and considerably more prep time for him to achieve, and reaching the point where he can just &quot;will&quot; such Effects into being would take much longer. Obviously the Spheres he actually learns will place practical limitations on what he can achieve in-game, but this question is about what is theoretically possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that your approach as a storyteller is definitely a valid one. I will consider what you have wrote, and write my thoughts and considerations about this later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 05-23-2020, 04:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-22T11:34:00-07:00","id":1390816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacecat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1390581-the-limitations-of-a-paradigm?p=1390789#post1390789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want to play a character who picks up magic from movies, TV, video games, and tabletop RPGs.<br /> <br /> Edit: and novels and comic books.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you mean this in the sense that their Awakening is a product of their exposure to these things, that they are significant parts of their Practices post-Awakening, or both? In any case, I think it's a cool concept <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> As noted above, I'm imagining this character as a chaos magician, with his Awakening possibly being tied to an epiphany around Magical Thinking reflecting on the power that the psychic constructs our societies create (egregores) have over us, and 'Awakening' to the idea of harnessing that. I'm imagining writing and speech, as focused expressions of Belief/Will and as a form of connection between minds, as being important Instruments for him. I also considered the Art of Desire as a Practice, but too much of that seems to be about social domination, which doesn't mesh with his attitudes about power and other people for the most part.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1390581-the-limitations-of-a-paradigm?p=1390791#post1390791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think your approach as a storyteller is definitely a valid one. I will consider what you have wrote, and write my thoughts and considerations about this later.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm honestly more considering this from the perspective of a player, as it's easier to gloss over the finicky details of a Focus/Paradigm with an NPC, but I am very glad that you think there's value in my perspective. I spent a lot of time browsing these forums anonymously before making an account, and I've often enjoyed yours and Aleph's perspectives on things, though I can't think of specific examples at the moment I'm afraid. I'm very pleased to say that I might have finally managed to put together a comprehensive model for the relationship between Spheres in this fellow's Paradigm, thanks to the contributions people have offered here <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Starting with Prime as the foundation, four 'Basic Spheres' emerge: the Basic Pattern Spheres of Matter and Forces, and the Basic Relational Spheres of Correspondence and Time.<br /> Each pair of Basic Spheres produces a 'Complex/Advanced Sphere' in combination: Life as the Complex Pattern Sphere, and Entropy as the Complex Relational Sphere.<br /> Mind exists at the top of the diamond/pyramid, the combination of Life and Entropy;<br /> Spirit meanwhile is the metaphysical substance/connections that holds all of it together, a sort of meta-Relational Sphere. (Kind of like the Force in Star Wars)<br /> <br /> Depending on how closely he's involved with the Traditions, he may or may not use their lingo around Patterns and Spheres, but these seems like a good model for his view of the world. His view is largely &quot;Everything is Chaos&quot; and &quot;Gods and Monsters&quot;; things just emerge from the raw possibility of Prime, with &quot;order&quot; and &quot;chaos&quot; simply being labels for what can be understood versus what can't, and &quot;good&quot; and &quot;evil&quot; only making sense from a given agenda or perspective. In his case, he chooses (generally) to be a benevolent 'God' rather than a horrible 'Monster,' but doesn't think it has anything to do with some higher justice or purpose.<br /> <br /> Putting aside that he simply views Mind as the most 'complex' component of the Tellurian, his Paradigm places a lot of emphasis on Mind to the extent that he largely considers it the source of Awakening/magick; it's his Affinity Sphere as a result. And though Life and Entropy are more 'complex' than their component Spheres in his framework, the closer proximity of Life and Entropy to Mind (being more closely tied to our human perspective) in his Paradigm means that they are the &quot;stepping stones&quot; to the Basic Spheres. However, I imagine his own Paradigm being (initially) focused more on the Relational Spheres; his early Spheres would likely follow a &quot;path&quot; from Mind &gt; Entropy &gt; Correspondence/Time &gt; Prime. Life would then be the 'path' to Matter and Forces. Spirit is going to be the &quot;missing link&quot; of his Paradigm that he would discover eventually through interaction with other Crafts/Traditions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","user":"Kharnov","date":". 05-22-2020, 02:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-23T01:24:20-07:00","id":1390930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1390581-the-limitations-of-a-paradigm?p=1390816#post1390816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> (...)<br /> Mind exists at the top of the diamond/pyramid, the combination of Life and Entropy;<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>(I'm sorry that I can't answer your post thoroughly, but I currently have some matters I need to sort out)<br /> I'd like to know about why you think the Mind kind of Magick should be at the top of this diamond/pyramid. This idea/concept seems to be interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 05-23-2020, 11:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-23T05:57:08-07:00","id":1390960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1390581-the-limitations-of-a-paradigm?p=1390816#post1390816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you mean this in the sense that their Awakening is a product of their exposure to these things, that they are significant parts of their Practices post-Awakening, or both?</div> </div> </div> </div>Both. And the character must be as accurate as possible to the media representation of the magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-23T08:17:26-07:00","id":1390975,"title":"","content":"It sounds like a pretty neat idea, Spacecat, but you will need to work within the framework of a somewhat-consistent set of Instruments and Practices; it might be a bit unfair if you just find some movie or TV show where wizards are depicted throwing fireballs willy-nilly and go &quot;I can do that!&quot; Like starting off with some sort of ritual centred around the media in question before being able to emulate more powerful Effects depicted within it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1390581-the-limitations-of-a-paradigm?p=1390930#post1390930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(I'm sorry that I can't answer your post thoroughly, but I don't currently have some matters I need to sort out)<br /> I'd like to know about why you think the Mind kind of Magick should be at the top of this diamond/pyramid. This idea/concept seems to be interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Understanding that what I'm describing is meant to be his Paradigm, and not a theory about how all Mage magic should work, I'd be glad to try and explain <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Mind is at the top of the pyramid for two reasons. The first is that &quot;the top of the pyramid&quot; isn't necessarily meant to say that Mind is significantly more powerful or more important than the other Spheres; it's simply understood to be more complex, within his framework. The four &quot;Basic Spheres&quot; are like atoms, the &quot;Advanced Spheres&quot; are like molecules, and Mind is like a cell.<br /> <br /> Of course, I will now contradict myself by admitting that Mind *is* especially important within his Paradigm, as the &quot;starting place&quot; of magic. In his Paradigm, Mind is necessary for two things; first, it provides the understanding necessary to comprehend *how* to perform magic, so he views it as closely tied to Awakening; secondly, he views magic as the process of converting mental/emotional energy into other forms of power to achieve the desired end, generally by using mental energy to subtly influence the underlying Prime. It's a little bit influenced by a layman's understanding of quantum physics, that perception has the power to tangibly influence outcomes.<br /> <br /> That's also why Matter and Forces are such difficult Spheres for him; compare getting a bunch of gold by tricking a person into giving it to you, or being able to subtly rig the rules of a game of chance, versus just thinking really hard at a rock to turn it into gold. Obviously, the fact that other Mages can do such things will eventually get across the possibility to him, but &quot;getting it&quot; will be more difficult for him I imagine.<br /> <br /> Also, just reflecting on this question has been helpful, as I realized there's at least a bit of a complication or shortcoming with my model: framing Mind as a combination of Life and Entropy comes with a bit of an issue when spirit-entities can have Minds without falling into the Life category. I have an answer; since Spirit is virtually everywhere within his pyramid/diamond model, it makes sense that it can roughly &quot;fill in&quot; for a lot of different things, like Life, when needed for a given Pattern.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-16T07:27:24-07:00","id":1403095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1390581-the-limitations-of-a-paradigm?p=1390975#post1390975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(...)<br /> That's also why Matter and Forces are such difficult Spheres for him; compare getting a bunch of gold by tricking a person into giving it to you, or being able to subtly rig the rules of a game of chance, versus just thinking really hard at a rock to turn it into gold. Obviously, the fact that other Mages can do such things will eventually get across the possibility to him, but &quot;getting it&quot; will be more difficult for him I imagine.</div> </div> </div> </div>The inverse could as well be true - If Mind is there at the 'top' for him, then shouldn't the minds of other persons be also quite difficult for him to influence?<br /> Like it has been said already, if Mind is at the top according to his Paradigm, then being able to throw lightning or transmutate items should be right up there in regard to his Magick. Mind over matter (and Forces <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) The question is how should him come to realizing it. I think you can deepen the Paradigm in one of two ways<br /> 1) He &quot;knew how to do it&quot; (channel Magick into Matter and Forces Effects) already, just lacked the familiarity to do this.<br /> 2) By focusing on the more 'intangible' Spheres first (Mind, Prime, Entropy) he actually started with the harder to achieve (within his deepened Paradigm) Effects, without realizing it at the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 07-16-2020, 10:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-21T10:17:56-07:00","id":1403836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1390581-the-limitations-of-a-paradigm?p=1403095#post1403095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The inverse could as well be true - If Mind is there at the 'top' for him, then shouldn't the minds of other persons be also quite difficult for him to influence?<br /> Like it has been said already, if Mind is at the top according to his Paradigm, then being able to throw lightning or transmutate items should be right up there in regard to his Magick. Mind over matter (and Forces <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) The question is how should him come to realizing it. I think you can deepen the Paradigm in one of two ways<br /> 1) He &quot;knew how to do it&quot; (channel Magick into Matter and Forces Effects) already, just lacked the familiarity to do this.<br /> 2) By focusing on the more 'intangible' Spheres first (Mind, Prime, Entropy) he actually started with the harder to achieve (within his deepened Paradigm) Effects, without realizing it at the time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hello! I am very sorry for taking so long to respond to you, I greatly appreciate your thoughtful contributions! (I am also a big fan of <i>Dune</i> and enjoy your username, if I have not said so before <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br /> <br /> The reasoning behind Matter and Forces (&quot;vulgar&quot; physical/material Effects of any kind, really) being especially difficult for him essentially ties in to a wonky blend of two different principles: the first is the concept of Cartesian mind-body/mental-physical dualism; the second is the concept from physics that any time energy is converted into another form, there is almost always energy &quot;lost&quot; as a consequence of it being converted to unusable forms as a side-effect of the process.<br /> <br /> The problem of Cartesian dualism is the &quot;interaction problem,&quot; the question of how these two forms of substance with completely different properties are supposed to be able to interact with each other. For this character's Paradigm, the solution is a Monism hiding beneath the Dualism, in the form of Prime. Material and mental are just two broad categories of forms that only interact with each other through the 'bridge' of Prime underneath everything.<br /> <br /> The problem of &quot;waste&quot; energy in conversion then explains why certain things are supposed to be easier, and other things more difficult. Because he believes that Magic starts on the &quot;mental&quot; side of the divide, Effects that are purely mental themselves are the easiest for him, because they require no conversion of the Mental Energy used to perform Magic in his Paradigm. Meanwhile, Effects that are &quot;subtle&quot; generally don't require more than one &quot;step&quot; of conversion, from Mental Energy to Primal Energy; in addition to the Effects of the Prime Sphere, affecting the underlying &quot;Prime energy field&quot; is how many Entropy Effects are achieved in his Paradigm. <br /> <br /> Subtle applications of Spheres like Correspondence, Time, Life, Matter, and Forces, can be explained either as Mental phenomena, simply providing knowledge, or even Primal, if the Effects are not extremely unreasonable. But &quot;vulgar&quot; Effects, explicit manipulation of &quot;material&quot; phenomena, is the most difficult because it requires an additional step of &quot;conversion,&quot; from Mental to Primal to Physical Energy, with a higher amount of &quot;wasted&quot; energy requiring a correspondingly higher investment, and a more difficult and complicated process overall.<br /> <br /> <br /> Going back to the topic of the pyramid, I should note that concept only came to me in response to the stimulation provided by this excellent thread. It is a bit of a separate phenomena from the difficulties described above, and in itself it doesn't really justify increased difficulty with Matter and Forces over Correspondence and Time, since both are equally distant from Mind within the model; it also puts Prime the &quot;furthest&quot; away, which would arguably make it the most difficult to learn or affect. But really, the pyramid model is supposed to reflect something else entirely. The pyramid is meant to be an explanatory model of a rise from simple Phenomena/Spheres to more complex Phenomena/Spheres. But the importance of Mind/Mental Phenomena within his Paradigm means that difficulty has less to do with the actual complexity of a Phenomena, but more to do with his familiarity or understanding of that Phenomena. <br /> <br /> Life and Entropy (it makes more sense it I steal the name &quot;Fate&quot; from <i>Awakening</i>) are closer to Mind than the more abstract/objective Phenomena of Matter, Forces, Time, and Correspondence(/Space) because they are a bigger, or better understood, part of our lived experience, our Mental existence. You feel blood coursing in your veins, your heart beating, your muscles and bones shifting. Similarly, an almost inevitable consequence of a Mental Existence is a concept of a 'Fate' for that Existence, a network of relations and interactions with other Existences you experience. In contrast, more basic Phenomena may be simpler, but they are less intuitive because they are not an intimate part of one's lived experience; you don't feel what it's like to be a rock or a bolt of lightning (normally), and our experience of Time tends to be highly subjective without the introduction of external measures and active effort to track its passage.<br /> <br /> It is, again, this concept of the importance of familiarity/understanding in the character's Paradigm that explains him having difficulties with Matter and Forces over Correspondence and Time; again, according to the pyramid model, all of them are equally &quot;distant&quot; from the starting point of Mind. His greater strength with Correspondence and Time over Matter and Forces has to do with him having been a liberal arts student rather than an engineer before his Awakening; while there are considerable influences of &quot;layman science&quot; on his Paradigm, his approach is ultimately more philosophical, and even spiritual, than scientific, which is why he isn't actually a techno-Mage. He'd actually be an almost perfect Batini if he was less individualistic and irreligious.<br /> <br /> (And heck yeah, Time + Correspondence mastery basically equals the Kwisatz Haderach, so again, I am a fan of <i>Dune</i> lol)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}